# Wall surface reactions for W divertor + SS chamber (approximated as W).
# Reads TRIM reflection tables from database/processes.h5:/surface/reflection/
# via surf_react surface/pwi.
#
# Channels evaluated in order; first to cross U~U[0,1] fires.
#  1) T <pair>   probability = R_N from TRIM table (reflected as same species)
#  2) A R [f]    absorb-and-re-emit; R = recycling fraction
#                (f optional for D+ atom->molecule partition; unused for W/O)
#
# W is an impurity: TRIM reflect only, no re-emit (particles that don't
# reflect are absorbed into the wall and dropped).
# O/D from the plasma recycle too (D recycles as D2, 95% partition).

# D+ recycling: neutralize + TRIM reflect as D, else absorb-and-re-emit as
# 95% D2 / 5% D (standard Franck-Condon partition).
D+ --> D
T d_on_w

D+ --> D2
A 0.99 0.95

D --> D
T d_on_w

D --> D2
A 0.99 0.95

D2 --> D2
A 0.99

# O recycling: TRIM reflect as atomic O, else absorbed (no O2 return).
O+ --> O
T o_on_w

O+ --> O
A 0.0

O --> O
T o_on_w

O --> O
A 0.0

# W reflection: TRIM reflect as neutral W, else absorbed (R=0 -> 100% pump).
# Every charge state needs both a T channel (reflect prob) and an A catch-all
# (unreflected W drops into the wall). Without the A channel, unreflected W
# would fall through to surf_collide diffuse and get thermally re-emitted.
W --> W
T w_on_w
W --> W
A 0.0

W+ --> W
T w_on_w
W+ --> W
A 0.0

W2+ --> W
T w_on_w
W2+ --> W
A 0.0

W3+ --> W
T w_on_w
W3+ --> W
A 0.0

W4+ --> W
T w_on_w
W4+ --> W
A 0.0

W5+ --> W
T w_on_w
W5+ --> W
A 0.0

W6+ --> W
T w_on_w
W6+ --> W
A 0.0

W7+ --> W
T w_on_w
W7+ --> W
A 0.0

W8+ --> W
T w_on_w
W8+ --> W
A 0.0

W9+ --> W
T w_on_w
W9+ --> W
A 0.0

W10+ --> W
T w_on_w
W10+ --> W
A 0.0

# W self-sputtering (W-on-W): additive Eckstein yield Y_WW(E_impact,theta).
# On each W-ion impact, emit floor(Y)+Bernoulli(frac Y) extra neutral W with a
# Thompson energy, ON TOP OF the T/A reflect/absorb outcome above. The impact
# energy is the sheath-boosted ion energy, so only energetic ions sputter
# (neutrals are sub-threshold). Sputtered W inherits the incident pweight.
W+ --> W
S W_on_W
W2+ --> W
S W_on_W
W3+ --> W
S W_on_W
W4+ --> W
S W_on_W
W5+ --> W
S W_on_W
W6+ --> W
S W_on_W
W7+ --> W
S W_on_W
W8+ --> W
S W_on_W
W9+ --> W
S W_on_W
W10+ --> W
S W_on_W
